@startuml
title Runtime and negotiated state reporting

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "Control application" as Client
participant "GATT service" as Gatt
participant "Runtime state collector" as State
participant "Bluetooth host" as Host
participant "Audio datapath" as Audio
participant "Bluetooth peer" as Peer

Client -> Gatt: Enable runtime_state notifications

Peer -> Host: ACL connection established
Host -> State: Connection ID and effective ACL parameters
State -> Gatt: runtime_state\n(validity bit 0)
Gatt -> Client: Notify connected state

Peer -> Host: PHY / data length updated
Host -> State: Effective TX/RX PHY and lengths
State -> Gatt: runtime_state\n(validity bits 0..2)
Gatt -> Client: Notify link state

Peer -> Host: ASE codec configuration
Host -> State: Negotiated LC3 configuration
State -> Gatt: runtime_state\n(validity bits 0..3)
Gatt -> Client: Notify codec-configured state

Peer -> Host: CIS QoS configuration
Host -> State: Negotiated ISO QoS and presentation delay
State -> Gatt: runtime_state\n(validity bits 0..5)
Gatt -> Client: Notify QoS-configured state

Peer -> Host: Stream enabled and started
Host -> Audio: Start audio datapath
Audio -> State: Streaming lifecycle state
State -> Gatt: runtime_state
Gatt -> Client: Notify streaming state

loop For each underrun episode or ACL policy adjustment
    Audio -> State: Updated underrun counter
    Host -> State: Effective ACL update, if changed
    State -> State: Increment sequence and adjustment counter
    State -> Gatt: runtime_state\n(validity bit 6)
    Gatt -> Client: Notify latest effective state
end

note over State,Client
Each notification identifies a session-local connection and stream.
The validity mask says which groups of fields may be interpreted.
end note
@enduml
